    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n31281" root="عيم" body-key="E">
    
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">عَيَامٌ</span></b>  The <i>day;</i> syn. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">نَهَارٌ</span>: (K:) mentioned by
Az, on the authority of El-Muärrij. (TA.) One
says, <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">طَابَ العِيَامُ</span> i. e. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">النَّهَارُ</span> [<i>The day became
pleasant</i>]. (TA.) [See <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">عَامٌ</span>, last sentence; in
art. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">عوم</span>.]

